  <section class="colophon" aria-labelledby="how">
    <div class="colophon-head"><h2 id="how">How it is built</h2><a class="down" href="#how-text" aria-label="Read how it is built"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v15M6 13l6 6 6-6"/></svg></a></div>
    <div id="how-text">
    <p>The shelf is plain CSS: each case is a 3D box (a hinged cover with the tracklist inside, spine, edges, a tray with the disc) under one <code>perspective</code>, and works out its place from its distance to the chosen one, <code>sibling-index()</code> less the choice: spine-on before it, fanned after it, forward at zero, with transitions carrying it there. The glossy floor is the shelf again, mirrored with <code>scaleY(-1)</code> and faded with a mask. <a href="https://reactivecss.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reactive CSS</a> adds the interaction, with no application JavaScript:</p>
    <ul><li>Two <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/state/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>state()</code></a>s, which case is chosen and whether it is open. <code>.case:on(click)</code> chooses <code>sibling-index()</code>, read at the event.</li><li><a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/drag/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>:on(drag)</code></a> along the shelf moves a case for every 70px of <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/event/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>event(delta-x)</code></a> from where the drag started; the arrow keys, Home and End step with <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/on-rule/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>:on(keydown(ArrowRight), prevent())</code></a>.</li><li>Enter or a click on the chosen case opens it: the cover swings open on its hinge and the disc slides out and spins; Escape closes it.</li><li>The glint sweeps across the chosen case only, and its disc spins only when open: one <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/when-selector/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>:when()</code></a> rule per place on the shelf.</li><li>The hint fades after the first browse, through a page-wide <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/state/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>state()</code></a> and <a href="https://reactivecss.com/docs/reference/when-selector/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>:when()</code></a>.</li></ul>
    </div>
